sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Web as Vue guest client
    participant API as Search routes / controller
    participant Search as Search application
    participant ES as Elasticsearch
    participant DB as MySQL repositories
    participant Redis as Redis
    participant Events as Event publisher / NATS

    opt User types a destination
        Web->>API: GET /api/v1/search/destinations/autocomplete
        API->>Search: getDestinationAutocomplete(text)
        Search->>ES: Query destinations suggestions
        ES-->>Search: Suggestions or no matches
        opt Elasticsearch unavailable or no suggestions
            Search->>DB: catalog.suggestDestinations(text)
            DB-->>Search: Destination suggestions
        end
        Search-->>API: Suggestions
        API-->>Web: 200 destination suggestions
    end

    Web->>Web: Submit dates and guests, update Router and Vuex
    opt New base search criteria in this page instance
        Web->>Web: Save recent search in localStorage
        Web->>API: POST /api/v1/search/log
        API->>Events: Publish search-performed event
        Events-->>API: Publish attempt completed, best effort
        API-->>Web: 201 log response
    end

    Web->>API: GET /api/v1/search/hotels with criteria, filters and page
    API->>API: Optional authentication and Joi validation
    API->>Search: searchHotels(params, userId)
    alt Valid explicit destinationId
        Search->>DB: catalog.getActiveDestinationById(id)
        DB-->>Search: Destination
    else Free-text destination or invalid id
        Search->>ES: Resolve normalized destination text
        ES-->>Search: Best city or country match
        opt No match or Elasticsearch error
            Search->>DB: catalog.findBestMatchDestinationByName(text)
            DB-->>Search: Destination or null
        end
    end
    Search->>Search: Calculate nights and total guests
    Search->>ES: Check ES health, search hotels index
    ES-->>Search: Candidate metadata
    opt ES unavailable, error, or zero hits for text location
        Search->>DB: Read hotel_search_snapshots with filters
        DB-->>Search: Fallback candidates
    end

    alt Candidate hotels exist
        Search->>DB: Check room inventory for every night
        DB-->>Search: Hotels satisfying rooms and capacity
        alt Available hotels exist
            loop Each available hotel, queried concurrently
                Search->>DB: Fetch available room types and date-specific prices
                DB-->>Search: Room details, stay totals and nightly averages
            end
            Search->>Search: Merge metadata and rooms, apply price filter
            Search->>Search: Rank, sort, build facets and paginate
            opt Signed in and page has hotels
                Search->>DB: identity.getFavoriteHotelIds(userId, pageHotelIds)
                DB-->>Search: Favorite IDs
            end
            Search->>Search: Attach is_favorite, false for anonymous guests
        else No hotels available for the stay
            Search->>Search: Format successful empty response
        end
    else No candidate hotels
        Search->>Search: Format successful empty response
    end

    Search-->>API: Search results and resolved destination ID/type
    opt Signed in
        API-)Redis: Record recent search, best effort, not awaited
    end
    API-)Events: Publish search-performed event, not awaited
    API-->>Web: 200 hotels, pagination, filter options and metadata
    Web->>Web: Render hotel cards or empty state
    Note over Web,API: Filter, sort and page changes repeat GET hotels. POST log is deduplicated by base criteria.
    Note over Events: NATS consumer is the Go analytics service, which writes MongoDB search_logs.
